# CS-0186 §17.4 rule 1, the ready-time half. The test's only source is the
# preceding step's `dist/**`, and that command creates a subdirectory and no
# file — so the declaration is non-empty and RESOLVES to nothing. Deciding
# "has this unit anything to key on?" at registration alone admits it and then
# keys it on nothing at all: its first verdict replayed for the life of the
# store, over a `probe.txt` it does read and nothing tracks.

recipe check
    cook "dist/**" { mkdir -p dist/sub }
    test { grep -q ok probe.txt }
